  "id": "rehgar",
  "name": "Rehgar",
  "role": "Healer",
  "overview": "Rehgar is a Healer with solid waveclear, the ability to clear Mercenary Camps on his own, and a powerful Trait to counter crowd control effects: Purge.",
  "strengths": [
    "Capable of clearing Mercenary Camps on his own very quickly",
    "High waveclear",
    "Option to use Ghost Wolf for in-combat mobility"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Lack of single-target sustain healing",
    "No access to hard crowd control and interrupts",
    "Low range on Purge to save allied Heroes without risk"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "sonya",
        "name": "Sonya"
      },
      {
        "id": "illidan",
        "name": "Illidan"
      },
      {
        "id": "greymane",
        "name": "Greymane"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Rehgar is a strong enabler for Bruisers (such as Sonya) and Melee Assassins (for example Illidan) because they benefit a lot from his whole kit: Lightning Shield is great on them, Ancestral Healing can be used to keep them alive, and Bloodlust provides them mobility, damage, and survivability."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "muradin",
        "name": "Muradin"
      },
      {
        "id": "varian",
        "name": "Varian"
      },
      {
        "id": "ana",
        "name": "Ana"
      },
      {
        "id": "tracer",
        "name": "Tracer"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Due to his limited single-target sustain healing, Rehgar is not that good against poke compositions who can whittle down a single target (usually the Tank) with constant damage.\n\nAlthough he is great against burst-compositions, some of them will have access to healing reduction effects (notably Biotic Grenade by Ana), which can partially or completely shut down his main anti-burst tool when timed correctly: Ancestral Healing."
  },
